1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,825
A ramp was built for wheelchair users, but parents with buggies and travellers with suitcases use it too. Accessible design helps everyone.

2
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:21,820
Some people use screen readers, some use only a keyboard, some zoom to two hundred percent. Design so all of them can finish the task.

3
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:32,520
The accessibility guidelines group everything under four ideas: perceivable, operable, understandable and robust.

4
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:41,120
Can people see or hear it? Can they use it with any input? Is it clear? Does it work with assistive tools?

5
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:47,570
Try your page with only the keyboard. Can you reach everything, and see where you are?

6
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:57,970
Use the right element and you get accessibility for free. A real button works with the keyboard. A clickable div does not.

7
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:05,570
Give icon buttons a name, keep headings in order, and add a skip link. Now fix the page.

